
You are a senior full-stack software engineer, product designer, database architect, and Android developer. Build a complete, production-minded personal productivity application called IRONMAN from scratch.

Do not create just a visual prototype. Build the real application, its screens, business logic, database, authentication, notifications, charts, data persistence, and Android integration.

If a project already exists, inspect it first and preserve useful code. If the project is empty, initialize it from scratch.

Do not stop after producing a plan. Implement the application. If you have filesystem and terminal access, create the actual project files, install dependencies, run checks, fix errors, and continue until the acceptance criteria are satisfied. If you cannot access a required external service or native build tool, explain exactly what is missing and still complete all work that can be implemented.

Do not ask unnecessary questions. Use the product requirements below as the source of truth.

==================================================
1. PRODUCT VISION
==================================================

App name: IRONMAN
Product type: Personal productivity, study, fitness, sleep, music, and expense tracking application.
Primary challenge duration: Three calendar months from a user-selected start date.
Default timezone: Asia/Tashkent.
Default currency: UZS.
Interface language: Uzbek, Latin alphabet.
Platforms: Desktop web browser and Android APK.
Primary user: A single individual managing their own study and fitness goals.

The two main goals are:

1. Improve personal fitness and consistently complete user-defined workouts.
2. Study SAT and English, record the topics to learn each day, and complete 10 mock tests.

Additional modules:
- Daily Dashboard
- SAT & English
- Fitness
- Sleep Tracker
- Music Playlists
- Expenses
- Analytics
- Settings and Profile

The experience must be simple, clean, motivating, professional, and practical to use every day.

The application should enforce discipline through daily deadlines, automatic missed-task handling, reminders, historical records, and analytics. It must not shame the user or fabricate successful progress.

Never invent study topics, workouts, expenses, sleep records, or mock scores. The user creates and records their own information.

